## Why a split license?

This follows the practice of the established game benchmarks WRYM learned
from (BALROG, LMGame-Bench, Baba Is AI, TextWorld — all MIT for code):
software and data have different natural licenses. Code is MIT so any
harness, fork, or evaluation stack can embed the engine with zero friction;
data is CC BY 4. so reused levels and results always trace back to the
certified ladder they came from.

Human-play exports from the WRYM Human Arena (schema `wyrm.humanrun/1`)
belong to the player who generated them. Sharing them back as community
results is welcome and counts as CC BY 4.0.
